<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I254dcbd3107ded523d3aef3e2b3429d3acbe9f84" commit="6955a59a1757eaf328f6a8a133ab76729fa3de79" commit_message="autotest: Add ebuild to build Python policy protos  Right now, every autotest that uses policy code compiles its own policy protos. There are over 30 nearly identical Makefiles for this.  This CL introduces an ebuild that generates the protos and puts them into autotest/client/protos/policy, along with __init__.py files for proper importing. The files are used by all policy autotests in the dependent CL, so there's no code duplication anymore.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:817437 BUG=chromium:793333 TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} login_OwnershipTaken login_OwnershipApi login_OwnershipRetaken TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} policy_ImagesAllowedForUrls --args='case=3Urls_Allow' TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} suite:policy suite:bvt-perbuild TEST=cros tryjob -g 817437 -g 817436 --hwtest chell-full  Change-Id: I254dcbd3107ded523d3aef3e2b3429d3acbe9f84 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/817436 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="817436" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="18" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/36/817436/18" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3b9596c022f2654c0360d1253c3bfbfa648635fc" commit="3d50a938239f983b93f86129518970abc190d353" commit_message="autotest: Refactor policy proto code  Right now, every autotest that uses policy code compiles its own policy protos. There are over 30 nearly identical Makefiles for this.  This CL reuses of the protos generated by the central ebuild in the dependent CL and gets rid of all the Makefiles. This is much cleaner and more efficient.  BUG=chromium:793333 TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} login_OwnershipTaken login_OwnershipApi login_OwnershipRetaken TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} policy_ImagesAllowedForUrls --args='case=3Urls_Allow' TEST=test_that -b ${BOARD} ${DUT_IP} suite:policy suite:bvt-perbuild TEST=cros tryjob -g 817437 -g 817436 --hwtest chell-full  CQ-DEPEND=CL:817436  Change-Id: I3b9596c022f2654c0360d1253c3bfbfa648635fc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/817437 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="817437" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/37/817437/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id9f1bfae1c5b5552d3c59fd0fd5b6e2d7388598c" commit="d9459198d4ecf38740bc87cc1b283cc6827488c7" commit_message="image_test: move security_RootfsStatefulSymlinks autotest here  This isn't a straight port of the existing autotest, but a rewrite.  The autotest does: - Search the rootfs for symlinks that point to known bad paths - Compare those symlinks against a whitelist - If the symlink is broken, and the whitelist sets can_dangle=true, ignore it - If the symlink is broken, and the whitelist sets can_dangle=false, fail - If the symlink isn't broken, compare the permissions of the target file   to the settings recorded in the whitelist  In practice, pretty much all symlinks are marked as can_dangle=true, so if the target doesn't exist when the test runs, we don't actually check the permissions.  The image test version instead does: - Search the rootfs for all symlinks - Resolve those symlinks against the rootfs - If any symlinks are broken, require them to be whitelisted - Don't perform any permission checks  The assumptions we operate on here: - Any mounts we do at runtime will be on empty directories, or otherwise   replicate the directory structure - Any symlinks we whitelist are responsible for the security of the target  So we gain better coverage by not requiring a blacklist of bad paths, but we lose the ability to check permissions of target files (not that we were doing that well in the autotest).  If we want to write a test to perform sanity checks on permissions in writable paths at runtime, we can do that independently of symlinks.  BUG=chromium:207625 TEST=`test_image chromiumos_image.bin FileSystemPermissionTest.TestRootfsSymlinks` passes CQ-DEPEND=CL:759080,CL:759082  Change-Id: Id9f1bfae1c5b5552d3c59fd0fd5b6e2d7388598c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/759119 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="759119" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/19/759119/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id022d3955686d695d88de15f373d8cf7cf52f77a" commit="fe2973115e0c1362bcdb39835dca5eb61991d47b" commit_message="firmware: Fix python import for cros_config_host  Fixing the import so the fake subpackage can be deleted.  BUG=None TEST=emerge-reef chromeos-firmware-reef  Change-Id: Id022d3955686d695d88de15f373d8cf7cf52f77a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/832994 Commit-Ready: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Tested-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="832994" owner_email="shapiroc@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform